sample.dll was written for these tests (MIT or Apache-2.0, like this crate),
to cover what plaso's test files lack: a PE32+ image with named,
ordinal-only and forwarded exports, an import by ordinal, a delay-loaded
import, a version resource, a named resource, resource directory time
stamps, a load configuration table and a CodeView (RSDS) record. It was
built from sample.c, sample.def, sample.rc, helper.def and user32.def by
build.sh with mingw-w64 on Debian 13 (gcc-mingw-w64-x86-64,
binutils-mingw-w64-x86-64, GNU ld 2.44); finish.py (Python standard library)
then sets what GNU ld leaves out: the delay import and load configuration
data directories, the resource directory time stamps and the checksum.
